  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Please let us set override statuses (Join/Online/Ask/Busy) for individual people on our friends lists...\n\nEver been guilt tripped into adding someone you don't know very well? Sometimes ignoring friend requests creates awkward moments in future encounters. What if you could add them and not have to worry about giving this stranger unrestricted access to your location and other friend circles without punishing the rest of your friends list by always staying on Orange or Red?\n\nOr maybe have you ever wanted some alone time while inviting the company of a select few, and wish you could show as available to them without opening yourself up to your entire friendslist?\n\nAllowing users to set individual statuses for friends, the system accommodates different relationship dynamics by...\n\n1. Ensuring that close friends have easier access while others must request permission.\n\n2. Reducing guilt or pressure to accept friend requests from acquaintances or strangers, as users can now control how accessible they are to different individuals.\n\n3. Providing a nuanced approach to privacy without resorting to complete invisibility or blanket red/orange statuses, fostering both community engagement and personal comfort.\n\nThoughts?",
